    "headline_prose": "The honest read is <strong>task-by-task, not a blanket winner</strong>. EPM is ahead on season-level prediction (frozen-preseason win-MAE <strong>6.26 vs 6.82</strong>) and playoff Brier (<strong>0.091 vs 0.102</strong>). The internal model <strong>leads</strong> EPM on game-margin RMSE (<strong>14.28 vs 14.07</strong>) &mdash; EPM is <em>not</em> strictly better on every task. They are <strong>tied</strong> on retro win-MAE, inside the &plusmn;0.05 noise band. The internal+EPM blend beats both on some rows; per an owner decision <strong>no EPM-RAPM blend ships</strong>, so it appears here only as an informative benchmark.",
    "darko_note": "<strong>DARKO daily</strong> is a per-game-date re-score at 96.1% player coverage &mdash; it is the like-for-like comparison for game margins, since our own board also updates daily. <strong>DARKO frozen</strong> is pre-season-frozen with no in-season update, so its frozen-preseason, retro and Brier cells are all measured pre-season-frozen and it is disadvantaged on the walk-forward game-margin row. The <strong>Blend</strong> column is benchmark-only &mdash; not a product.",
    "darko_daily_coverage": 0.961,
